 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1790). Words follow the Peters engraving's spelling and punctuation (leggiadri. with a full stop, Eh via non fate. with no ellipsis, Io burlo, io burlo?, davvero as one word, Oh Dei!, and the asides in brackets). Dorabella's “Due, se volete” is printed “Duc se volete” (bar 38), a misprint; the word keeps the printed letters so that it lines up with the score, and its IPA and meaning are those of due. Ferrando's raccomandai (bar 12) and Dorabella's Dei (bar 54) are sung in more syllables than usual, and their IPA follows the score. IPA, word meanings and translations come from the app's reviewed Così libretto drafts (L47, IPA checked against Castel). IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
